{
  "name": "wall_peek",
  "note": "(anim-rework S5 keys, real-world standard, keyed by hand; never traced) Back to the wall, standing, the peek at the RIGHT edge (the left is mirrored): the lean comes from the hips and the outside knee, not the neck alone: the pelvis shifts 7 cm toward the edge and dips 5 deg on that side over a more bent right knee (40 deg, the foot a little out) while the left leg stays longer (32 deg), the trunk tips toward the edge (spine 6, chest 12 deg) and the head turns 55 deg round it, held a little more upright than the chest, so the head and one eye go past the edge (the body stays at the edge marker). Held with two slow breaths and a small in-out of 1.5 cm. Not mirrored. Angles in degrees in the body frame (x right, y up, z forward): pitch about x (+ the top forward), yaw about y (+ turns right), roll about z (+ the right side up). Pelvis offsets in cm from the standing rest. Arms: flex (+ forward, in the chest frame: the world angle is flex minus the chest pitch), abd (+ out), elbow (+ bent), inward; wrist (anim-rig, RIG.md) yaw / pitch / roll in the forearm frame, right hand as written, the left mirrored. Holstered arms; with a weapon drawn the arms stay procedural. Legs (the Blender preview and the track only: the game's feet come from the foot planner): flex (+ the knee forward), add (+ the foot in toward the midline), knee (+ bent), ankle (+ the toes up).",
